This function is already very small, so the change is micro-level. It reads `type` and `profile` into locals once, and adds a branch hint (`__builtin_expect`) for the common case where `type` is already set. Results are unchanged for every input.

```cpp
FIT_UINT8 Field::GetType() const
{
    const FIT_UINT8 t = type;
    if (__builtin_expect(t != FIT_UINT8_INVALID, 1))
        return t;

    const auto* p = profile;
    if ((p == NULL) || (profileIndex >= p->numFields))
        return FIT_UINT8_INVALID;

    return p->fields[profileIndex].type;
}
```